From a8a9b212eb9f573a03209be2d9ad75bee067b805 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashwin Goyal <letthedreamersrise@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:04:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(uniswap-v4): charge the protocol fee per swap direction
 and keep it under hook LP fee overrides

The v4 protocol fee is packed per direction in slot0.protocolFee (zeroForOne in
the low 12 bits, oneForZero in the next 12), but the tracker folded only the
zeroForOne half into SwapFee, which the simulator then used for both
directions. A pool with a oneForZero-only protocol fee was quoted without it,
and a zeroForOne-only fee was charged on oneForZero swaps too.

On dynamic-fee pools a hook's BeforeSwap LP fee replaced the whole swap fee,
dropping the protocol fee, whereas PoolManager.swap applies
ProtocolFeeLibrary.calculateSwapFee to the overriding LP fee. An override to
0 was also ignored because only a non-zero SwapFee counted as an override.

- ToExtra stores slot0's packed protocolFee and lpFee as `pF` / `lpF`, only
  while the protocol fee is on, so the Extra of every other pool is unchanged.
- The simulator computes each quote's fee from the swap direction: the LP fee
  (a dynamic-fee pool's hook override, else slot0.lpFee) combined with that
  direction's protocol fee. Without `pF` (protocol fee off, or an Extra written
  before this change) SwapFee is used as before.
- A BeforeSwap SwapFee carrying OverrideFeeFlag (LPFeeLibrary's
  OVERRIDE_FEE_FLAG, 0x400000) overrides the LP fee even when it is 0. A bare
  non-zero SwapFee keeps overriding as it did, and a bare 0 still means no
  override.
- SwapFee is unchanged (the zeroForOne fee).

Tests use amounts from v4-core's PoolManager.swap on the same pools.

